# Brunnwinkl boathouse (Bootshaus, back-layer prop over the shore block,
# D-031/D-038): a steep wooden-shingle roof (O shingles, l joints, 1 px l drip
# shadows, courses offset 2 px; o/O lit left barge board, l right) over a short o/O
# plank wall with a cross window, on o O l stilts over the
# dark d slip where a white rowing boat (w i m) hangs on two l hoist slings
# (the lake itself is the jetty/jetty_post tiles below the prop).
# Left of it a plank stair tower and a woodpile form the 2-tile steps.
# Drawn = solid: the outline matches the collision profile in tiles (prop
# placed bottom centre under col 223 + dx 8, bottom = top of the jetty row):
#   x  0-15 (col 221) woodpile, top lip y 48  -> 2 tiles above the jetty;
#   x 16-31 (col 222) stair tower, top lip y 16 -> 4 tiles;
#   x 32-95 (cols 223-226) roof ridge, o lip y 0 -> 5 tiles (the launch).
# Stilts sit at x 6-8 of each tile like jetty_post, so jetty_post tiles under
# it continue them into the lake. Back layer: no k, no outlines.
# Generated by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grid is the source.
sprite = boathouse
size   = 96x80
origin = 48,80
anim   = idle frames=1
---
frame idle 0
